| 1 | `custom_strdup` | no options; empty string (`str[0] == 0`), allocation/copy size 1 | [ ] |\n| 2 | `custom_strdup` | no options; one non-NUL byte followed by NUL, allocation/copy size 2 | [ ] |\n| 3 | `custom_strdup` | no options; many non-NUL ASCII bytes followed by NUL | [ ] |\n| 4 | `custom_strdup` | no options; many arbitrary non-NUL bytes (including high-bit bytes) followed by NUL | [ ] |\n| 5 | `custom_strdup` | no options; NUL-terminated prefix followed by additional bytes, proving the first NUL determines the result | [ ] |\n\nThe generic null-pointer case is invalid and is tracked in `ERRORS.md`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
